<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="u1b-ct-labeled">
  <title>Unit 1b Subgoal Labeled Puzzles for Toggle Code</title>
  <p>
    These are copies of the Mixed Up Code Practice 1b puzzles with subgoal
    labels added. The Unit 1b Toggle Code Practice page uses them as the Get
    Help puzzles for its write code problems. Problems whose solution has
    fewer than two subgoals keep the original, unlabeled puzzle.
  </p>

  <activity label="u1bex1muc-sgl" xml:id="u1bex1muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print a random number from
        1 to 50. But, the blocks have been mixed up and may include an extra
        block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks from the
        left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check
        button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="1">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Pick a random whole number in the range</cline>
          <cline>        int num = (int)(Math.random() * 50) + 1;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Pick a random whole number in the range</cline>
          <cline>        int num = (int) Math.random() * 50 + 1;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Pick a random whole number in the range</cline>
          <cline>        int num = (int)(Math.random() * 50);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Pick a random whole number in the range</cline>
          <cline>        int num = Math.random() * 50 + 1;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>        // Display the random number</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(num);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1bex2muc-sgl" xml:id="u1bex2muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print the first 2
        characters of the message followed by the last 2 characters of the
        message. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include an extra block
        that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks from the left
        and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the Check button
        to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="7">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>        // Store the message</cline>
        <cline>        String message = "I hope this works";</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Get the start of the message</cline>
          <cline>        String part1 = message.substring(0,2);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Get the start of the message</cline>
          <cline>        String part1 = message.substring(0,1);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Get the end of the message</cline>
          <cline>        String part2 = message.substring(message.length() - 2);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Get the end of the message</cline>
          <cline>        String part2 = message.substring(message.length() - 2, message.length() - 1);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Combine the start and end</cline>
          <cline>        String ends = part1 + part2;</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Combine the start and end</cline>
          <cline>        String ends = part1 * part2;</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>        // Display the combined start and end</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(ends);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1bex3muc-sgl" xml:id="u1bex3muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print the initials in
        lowercase letters. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include an
        extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks
        from the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the
        Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="4">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <cline>        // Store the names</cline>
        <cline>        String first = "Gerald";</cline>
        <cline>        String middle = "Foster";</cline>
        <cline>        String last= "Jones";</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>        // Get the first letter of each name</cline>
        <cline>        String initials = first.substring(0,1) +</cline>
        <cline>                          middle.substring(0,1) +</cline>
        <cline>                          last.substring(0,1);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Change the first letters into lowercase</cline>
          <cline>        String lowerInitials = initials.toLowerCase();</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Change the first letters into lowercase</cline>
          <cline>        initials.toLowerCase();</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Display the lowercase letters</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.println(lowerInitials);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Display the lowercase letters</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.println(initials);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1bex4muc-sgl" xml:id="u1bex4muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print the message in all
        uppercase letters. But, the blocks have been mixed up and include an
        extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the needed blocks
        from the left and put them in the correct order on the right. Click the
        Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="3">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <cline>      // Store the message</cline>
        <cline>      String message = "Don't Pokemon and drive!";</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>      // Change the message into uppercase</cline>
          <cline>      String upperMessage = message.toUpperCase();</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>      // Change the message into uppercase</cline>
          <cline>      message.toUpperCase();</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>      // Display the uppercase message</cline>
          <cline>      System.out.println(upperMessage);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>      // Display the uppercase message</cline>
          <cline>      System.print(upperMessage);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>      // Display the uppercase message</cline>
          <cline>      System.out.println(message);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1bex5muc-sgl" xml:id="u1bex5muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print the first 3 letters
        of message in uppercase letters. But, the blocks have been mixed up and
        include an extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag the
        needed blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the
        right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="7">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="5">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>        // Store the message</cline>
        <cline>        String message = "Have a nice day!";</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="6">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Get the start of the message</cline>
          <cline>        String part = message.substring(0,3);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Get the start of the message</cline>
          <cline>        String part = message.substring(0,4);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Change the start into uppercase</cline>
          <cline>        String upper = part.toUpperCase();</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Change the start into uppercase</cline>
          <cline>        part.toUpperCase();</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Display the uppercase letters</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.println(upper);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Display the uppercase letters</cline>
          <cline>        System.out.println(part);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>

  <activity label="u1bex6muc-sgl" xml:id="u1bex6muc-sgl" numbered="yes" adaptive="yes" indentation="hide" language="java">
    <statement>
      <p>
        The main method in the following class should print the part of the
        message starting with the word “nice”. But, the blocks have been mixed
        up and include an extra block that isn’t needed in the solution. Drag
        the needed blocks from the left and put them in the correct order on the
        right. Click the Check button to check your solution.
      </p>
    </statement>

    <blocks>
      <block order="6">
        <cline>public class Test1</cline>
        <cline>{</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="1">
        <cline>    public static void main(String[] args)</cline>
        <cline>    {</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="3">
        <cline>        // Store the message</cline>
        <cline>        String message = "Have a nice day!";</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="2">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Find where the word starts in the message</cline>
          <cline>        int pos = message.indexOf("nice");</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Find where the word starts in the message</cline>
          <cline>        int pos = message.indexof("nice");</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="7">
        <choice correct="yes">
          <cline>        // Get the part of the message starting at the word</cline>
          <cline>        String part = message.substring(pos);</cline>
        </choice>
        <choice>
          <cline>        // Get the part of the message starting at the word</cline>
          <cline>        String part = message.substring(0, pos);</cline>
        </choice>
      </block>

      <block order="8">
        <cline>        // Display the part of the message</cline>
        <cline>        System.out.println(part);</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="4">
        <cline>    } // end main method</cline>
      </block>

      <block order="9">
        <cline>} // end of class</cline>
      </block>
    </blocks>
  </activity>
</section>
